---
// "The importance of grandparents" — narrative section pairing a sticky
// close-up photograph with scroll-revealed editorial copy about
// experience, unconditional love, family memory, and dignified aging.
import Photo from "../components/Photo.astro"
import { importanceImage } from "../data/images"
---

<section
  class="bg-background-alt py-section"
  id="purpose"
  aria-labelledby="importance-heading"
>
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-landing px-container-x sm:px-8 xl:px-14">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:gap-20">
      <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
        <Photo image={importanceImage} ratio="1 / 1" class="max-w-md" />
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
        <div>
          <p
            class="mb-4 font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-muted uppercase"
          >
            Why this matters
          </p>
          <h2
            id="importance-heading"
            class="max-w-heading text-balance text-headline-2 leading-tight font-semibold text-foreground"
            data-split-reveal
          >
            Grandparents carry what no book can teach.
          </h2>
        </div>

        <p class="reveal max-w-copy text-lg text-muted">
          A grandparent's experience isn't nostalgia — it's a working memory of
          the family, held by someone who has already survived what the rest of
          us are still learning. That knowledge disappears quietly when it goes
          unheard.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal max-w-copy text-lg text-muted">
          Their love tends to ask for very little in return. It is patient in a
          way few relationships still are, and it gives children a sense of
          belonging to something older than themselves — a family, a history, a
          place they came from.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal max-w-copy text-lg text-muted">
          Aging with dignity doesn't require heroics. It requires being seen,
          consulted, and included — not managed from a distance. That is the
          standard we work toward with every family we support.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
